  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$",
  "worked_solution": "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}k+9 \\\\ 2k+18\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}k+9=0 \\\\ 2k+18=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=-9.$",
